    New tooling to support working on documentation locally

    - Added a bash script to build documentation locally and save logs into a log file with incremental number: `build-docs-locally.sh`
        - Run it in bash using the command below:
            ```bash
            bash build-docs-locally.sh
            ```
        - Or run it using the new task `build and serve docs` in `tasks.json` that calls the script
            - This task will also serve the documentation locally after building it

    - Added a bash script to serve pre-built documentation locally: `serve-pre-built-docs.sh`
        - Run it in bash using the command below:
            ```bash
            bash serve-pre-built-docs.sh
            ```
        - Or run it using the new task `serve pre-built docs` in `tasks.json` that calls the script
        - Port 8000 is explicitly set

    - Added a bash script to update all examples automatically: `update_all_examples.sh`
            - Run it in bash using the command below:
                ```bash
                bash update_all_examples.sh
                ```
            - Or run it using the new task `Update all examples` in `tasks.json` that calls the script

    - Added a bash script to update current example automatically: `update_current_example.sh`
            - Run it in bash using the command below:
                ```bash
                bash update_current_example.sh "path/to/notebook.ipynb"
                ```
            - Or run it using the new task `Update current example` in `tasks.json` that calls the script and passes the current file path as an argument

    - Added a new task to build docs, serve them and watch for changes using `sphinx-autobuild` in `tasks.json`
        - Run it using the new task `build and serve docs and watch for changes` in `tasks.json`
        - This task will build the documentation, serve it locally and watch for changes to automatically rebuild and refresh the browser
        - Port 8000 is explicitly set

    - Scripts `update_all_examples.sh` and `update_current_example.sh` run jupyter nbconvert to execute notebooks and then clean up unnecessary notebook and cell metadata using `nb-clean` while preserving important metadata for documentation at the website
    - For more information on using tasks in VS Code, please refer to the official documentation: https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/editor/tasks or https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/editing/tips-and-tricks#_task-runner

